          "Following systemic abuses where executives adopted plans and dumped stock days before catastrophic earnings warnings, the SEC adopted sweeping reforms. Modern Rule 10b5-1 plans enforce strict Mandatory Cooling-Off Periods: for directors and officers, trades cannot execute until the later of (1) 90 days following plan adoption/modification, or (2) 2 business days following the filing of Form 10-Q or Form 10-K covering the fiscal quarter in which the plan was adopted (subject to a maximum 120 days).",
