        "answerIndex": 1,
        "explanation": "Under 11 U.S.C. \u00a7 1516(c) and international UNCITRAL jurisprudence, the presumption that the registered office is the debtor's COMI is strictly rebuttable. Courts evaluate where the debtor conducts regular administration ascertainable by third parties (creditors).",
        "why": "Understanding COMI prevents corporate debtors from engaging in bad-faith jurisdictional arbitrage and ensures that cross-border debt restructurings are administered by the court with the most legitimate economic connection to the enterprise.",
          answer: 1
